WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.280
A warning light only knows about the car.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.270
It has no idea who is driving it.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.930
Car Neuron is a vehicle agent that reads both.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.574
A blackbox streams engine data once a second.

00:00:13.574 --> 00:00:17.290
A webcam watches the driver, right in the browser.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:23.130
One agent reads everything, explains what's wrong, and says what to do next.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.610
Same fault, different advice, depending on who's behind the wheel.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.953
Here's how it works.

00:00:31.953 --> 00:00:34.060
The browser does the sensing.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:39.581
Every second it makes a blackbox record, and fifteen records make one batch.

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:42.196
The car's data is simulated for now;

00:00:42.196 --> 00:00:44.230
everything after it is real.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:51.411
The camera runs MediaPipe locally, and only a small JSON event ever leaves the tab.

00:00:51.411 --> 00:00:52.216
No frames.

00:00:52.216 --> 00:00:53.263
No landmarks.

00:00:53.263 --> 00:00:56.080
The schema rejects any extra field.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.762
On the server, safety never waits for a model.

00:00:59.762 --> 00:01:03.151
Plain rules set the level and the mandatory step.

00:01:03.151 --> 00:01:08.270
Coolant at one hundred twenty degrees is critical, whatever the AI thinks.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:18.940
The same Guardian policy is written twice, in Python and in TypeScript, and both are tested against one table of cases, so they can't drift apart.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.639
Then an LLM agent, through In World Router, does what rules can't.

00:01:24.639 --> 00:01:25.820
It calls tools:

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:35.430
outside weather, maintenance history, nearby garages, and a booking proposal that stays pending until the driver confirms.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:40.642
Finally, the plan combines the car's level with the driver's state.

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:43.244
A warning with an alert driver means:

00:01:43.244 --> 00:01:44.228
book a garage.

00:01:44.228 --> 00:01:47.323
The same warning with a drowsy driver means:

00:01:47.323 --> 00:01:51.050
stop and rest first, and no booking is ever proposed.

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:58.050
The answer is spoken by Blaze, in the driver's language, and shown by a small robot in the corner.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.311
What broke?

00:02:01.311 --> 00:02:02.269
First, speed.

00:02:02.269 --> 00:02:08.830
The agent takes ten to twenty seconds to answer, and a tired driver can't wait that long.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:14.270
So the rules speak first, within a few seconds, and the plan comes after.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.608
Then, noise.

00:02:15.608 --> 00:02:20.050
Clips overlapped, and the same warning repeated every batch.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:26.120
Now each alert is claimed once per episode, and a critical clip cuts a milder one.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.115
Then the model and the rules disagreed.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:36.684
The agent once called a drowsy driver critical when the car was only warning, and the plan sent them to a tow truck.

00:02:36.684 --> 00:02:40.730
Now the plan asks the hard rules about the car, not the model.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.810
Small things hurt too.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:48.959
Blaze's download answers "too early" until the audio is ready, so we keep checking.

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:54.960
An English screen spoke Vietnamese, so each language got its own agent and voice.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:03:03.038
And a robot animating beside the 3D car slowed navigation from a fifth of a second to ten.

00:03:03.038 --> 00:03:05.920
Without a GPU, it now holds still.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.385
The trade-off:

00:03:07.385 --> 00:03:12.460
we chose the pro voice model for quality, and fixed latency elsewhere.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:13.364
Next:

00:03:13.364 --> 00:03:22.710
a real car through the O B D gateway, head-turn checks on real faces, and one LLM call after the tools.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.113
The lesson:

00:03:24.113 --> 00:03:27.840
let rules guard, and let the model explain.
